---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
const email = 'contact@sobiinteractive.com';
---
<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  updated="19 November 2026"
  description="How SOBI Interactive collects, uses and protects personal data on its website and in its mobile games."
>
  <p>This Privacy Policy explains how SOBI Interactive collects, uses and protects personal data when you visit sobiinteractive.com, contact us, or play our mobile games on Android and iOS.</p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>SOBI Interactive is the game brand of <strong>Sophia Business Innovation Company Limited</strong> (Công ty TNHH Sophia Business Innovation), a company registered in Vietnam under enterprise code 0801511006. The company is the controller of the personal data described in this policy.</p>
  <p>Contact for all privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>

  <h2>2. Data we collect on this website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact form.</strong> When you send the form on our Partners page, we receive what you enter: your company name, your name, email address, country, how you would like to work with us, and the kind of games you are looking for. The form is delivered to our mailbox by Web3Forms, a form delivery service.</li>
    <li><strong>Email.</strong> When you email us, we receive your email address and the content of your message.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data.</strong> Our hosting provider processes standard server data such as IP address, browser type and the pages requested, in order to deliver and secure the website.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This website does not use advertising cookies or tracking cookies.</p>

  <h2>3. Data we collect in our games</h2>
  <p>Our games are designed to work without asking for your name, email address or phone number. When you play, the following data may be processed:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Device and app data:</strong> device model, operating system version, language, country, app version and crash reports.</li>
    <li><strong>Gameplay data:</strong> levels played, session length, progress and in-game settings, used to improve the game and balance difficulty.</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising identifiers:</strong> the Google Advertising ID on Android or the Identifier for Advertisers (IDFA) on iOS, used to show ads, measure them and limit how often you see the same ad. On iOS we only access the IDFA if you allow it through Apple's App Tracking Transparency prompt.</li>
    <li><strong>Purchase data:</strong> if you buy items inside a game, the purchase is processed by Google Play or the App Store. We receive a confirmation of the purchase, not your payment card details.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Some of this data is processed by third-party services built into our games, such as advertising networks, analytics tools and crash reporting tools. These providers handle data under their own privacy policies. The services used by each game are disclosed in its Google Play Data safety section and its App Store privacy details.</p>

  <h2>4. How we use data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to your messages and evaluate partnership enquiries.</li>
    <li>To run, maintain and improve our games, fix bugs and balance gameplay.</li>
    <li>To show advertising that keeps our games free to play, and to measure it.</li>
    <li>To process and restore in-game purchases.</li>
    <li>To protect our services against fraud and abuse, and to meet our legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal data.</p>

  <h2>5. Legal basis</h2>
  <p>We process personal data with your consent (for example, when you send our contact form or allow ad tracking), to perform our agreement with you when you play our games or make a purchase, for our legitimate interests in running and improving our services, and to comply with the law. We apply the personal data protection rules of Vietnam and, where they apply to you, the rights given by laws such as the EU and UK GDPR and Californian privacy law.</p>

  <h2>6. How long we keep data</h2>
  <p>We keep contact form submissions and emails for as long as needed to handle the enquiry and any partnership that follows, and for no longer than three years after our last contact unless the law requires longer. Game data is kept for as long as it is needed for the purposes above and is then deleted or made anonymous.</p>

  <h2>7. International transfers</h2>
  <p>Our service providers may process data in countries outside Vietnam, including the United States and the European Union. When this happens, we rely on the safeguards offered by those providers.</p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us to access, correct or delete your personal data, to restrict or object to its processing, to receive a copy of it, or to withdraw your consent at any time. You can also limit ad personalisation in your device settings: on Android under Settings, Google, Ads; on iOS under Settings, Privacy &amp; Security, Tracking.</p>
  <p>To delete data from one of our games, follow the steps on our <a href="/data-deletion">Data Deletion</a> page. For any other request, email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. We reply within 30 days.</p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>Our website and games are not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from them. If you believe a child has given us personal data, contact us and we will delete it.</p>

  <h2>10. Security</h2>
  <p>We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect personal data, including encrypted connections and limited access. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, but we work to protect your data.</p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy when our services or the law change. The date at the top of this page shows the latest version. If a change is significant, we will make it clear on this website or in our games.</p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>Sophia Business Innovation Company Limited (SOBI Interactive), Vietnam. Email: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
